@base = http://127.0.0.1:8081
@fault1 = http://127.0.0.1:8081
@fault2 = http://127.0.0.1:8082
@fault3 = http://127.0.0.1:8083
@proxy = http://127.0.0.1:8084

### Fault 1A — known virtual host succeeds
GET {{fault1}}/healthz HTTP/1.1
Host: status.campuspulse.example

### Fault 1B — same socket, unknown Host fails
GET {{fault1}}/healthz HTTP/1.1
Host: www.campuspulse.example

### Fault 2A — redirect loop at the site root
GET {{fault2}}/ HTTP/1.1
Host: campuspulse.example

### Fault 2B — legacy POST receives a 302 redirect
POST {{fault2}}/legacy/incidents HTTP/1.1
Host: campuspulse.example
Content-Type: application/json

{"service":"library-wifi"}

### Fault 2C — target endpoint accepts POST directly
POST {{fault2}}/api/incidents HTTP/1.1
Host: campuspulse.example
Content-Type: application/json

{"service":"library-wifi"}

### Fault 3A — proxy path loops because the app never sees X-Forwarded-Proto
GET {{proxy}}/healthz HTTP/1.1
Host: campuspulse.example

### Fault 3B — app direct, no forwarded protocol
GET {{fault3}}/healthz HTTP/1.1
Host: campuspulse.example

### Fault 3C — app direct with the one header it expected
GET {{fault3}}/healthz HTTP/1.1
Host: campuspulse.example
X-Forwarded-Proto: https
